<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Vive le vent (Francis Blanche)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new French words about winter and the New Year</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ein kleiner weißer Schneemann (Roy Black)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, German words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Jingle Bells, Batman Smells</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">mid-1960s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Jingle Bells, Shotgun Shells</span><span class="sg-chain-h">children's parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Yingle Bells (Yogi Yorgesson)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Rusty Chevrolet (Da Yoopers)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Aussie Jingle Bells (Colin Buchanan)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody, set in the Australian summer</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Jingle Bell Drag (The Three Stooges)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Jingle Bombs (Jeff Dunham)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Pumpkin Bells, in The Peanuts Book of Pumpkin Carols</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1960s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody for Halloween</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Jingle Bell Rock (Bobby Helms)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">homage, with a different melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Tintinabulations (Katherine W. Punwar)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement for full orchestra</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">It's Beginning to Look a Lot Like Christmas (Bing Crosby)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">opening notes of the chorus quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Christmas Song (Nat King Cole)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in a guitar passage</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Merry Christmas Baby (Bruce Springsteen)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in a saxophone solo by Clarence Clemons</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Santa Claus Is Comin' to Town (Bruce Springsteen)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted on piano at the end</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Green Chri$tma$ (Stan Freberg)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1957</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">When Christmas Comes (Mariah Carey)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">River (Joni Mitchell)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1971</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted on piano at the opening</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Sleighing songs of the 1850s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">similar lines, as argued by Kyna Hamill</span></li></ul></section>
